WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:06.480
It was an ordinary night at Site 19 and Dr.
Smith was hard at work in his office.

00:00:06.480 --> 00:00:11.600
The overhead light was just about ready to
give out, the bulb dim and flickering, but

00:00:11.600 --> 00:00:15.920
there was no one available to change it at
the moment so he would just make do.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:18.880
Besides, he only had a little bit of work
left to finish.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:23.600
Hunched over his desk, eyes bleary and head
aching from too many hours of staring at a

00:00:23.600 --> 00:00:28.240
screen, he was ready to wrap up this report
and finally get home for some well-deserved

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:28.960
rest.

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:33.280
The constant anxiety of working with some
of the scariest monsters in the world was

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:38.240
one thing, but the hours spent writing paperwork
on the monsters was an altogether different

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:39.920
kind of terrifying.

00:00:39.920 --> 00:00:44.640
Most of the research staff had left for the
night, and only Dr. Smith and the usual security

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.320
team remained in the building.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:51.680
There was no sound except the click of his
fingers on the keys, his occasional exhausted

00:00:51.680 --> 00:00:57.280
sigh, and the infrequent sound of footsteps
in the hall outside as a security officer

00:00:57.280 --> 00:00:58.800
made his rounds.

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:03.760
Dr. Smith leaned back in his chair, stretching
his arms over his head and feeling his back

00:01:03.760 --> 00:01:04.480
crack.

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:05.680
Almost done.

00:01:05.680 --> 00:01:10.160
He recalled, dimly, a thermos of tea he had
left on the shelf behind him.

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:14.400
Perhaps that would be the kick he needed to
finish this work up and get home to his bath,

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:17.120
his books, and his pet cat Roger.

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:21.440
He swiveled his chair around, preparing to
stand up and retrieve the thermos when he

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:24.560
suddenly came face to face with a nightmare.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:31.760
There, less than an inch from him, was a smooth
featureless face, black as the night and devoid

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:33.600
of any expression.

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:39.520
It was hunched over, its face peering into
him, despite not having any eyes itself.

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:44.720
Without a sound, without so much as a creak
of the door, this thing had come into his

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:49.600
office and appeared behind him, waiting for
him to turn around and see it.

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:54.320
Dr. Smith let out a shriek of terror, knocking
his chair over as he scrambled to get away

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:55.520
from the intruder.

00:01:55.520 --> 00:02:00.160
His heart pounding in his ears, he tore past
the dark figure, yanking open the door to

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:03.360
his office and taking off running down the
hall.

00:02:03.360 --> 00:02:07.600
He called out for help, for someone, anyone,
to come.

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:11.680
Several security personnel heard his cries
and rushed to see what had happened.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:16.880
They found a shivering Dr. Smith, babbling
about a “demon” in his office and repeating

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:20.320
“it doesn’t have a face” over and over
again.

00:02:20.320 --> 00:02:24.880
Once he had calmed down - and finally been
given that cup of tea - Dr. Smith was informed

00:02:24.880 --> 00:02:30.000
that as stressful as that encounter might
have been, he was never really in any danger.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:34.800
We don’t have another SCP-173 on our hands
here, thankfully.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:37.840
This statue isn’t murderous or even violent.

00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:42.960
To the best of our observational ability,
we’ve determined that this particular surprisingly

00:02:42.960 --> 00:02:46.240
mobile statue is just kind of a jerk.

00:02:46.240 --> 00:02:52.880
SCP-650, nicknamed “The Startling Statue,”
is a stylized black statue of a humanoid figure,

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:56.080
standing at 167 centimeters tall.

00:02:56.080 --> 00:03:01.760
It has no hands or facial features, its arms
ending in rounded points, and its face and

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:04.720
head a smooth surface like that of a mannequin.

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:09.600
When the statue is dormant, or at least resting
and waiting for its next chance to move, it

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:15.120
stands straight and reaches upwards, head
tilted up as if its nonexistent eyes are watching

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:16.160
the sky.

00:03:16.160 --> 00:03:21.040
Attempts to determine the materials the statue
is made of have proved inconclusive.

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:25.600
Some tests show an impossibly large combination
of different materials, where other tests

00:03:25.600 --> 00:03:29.840
came back with no matches for any recognized
materials at all.

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:34.400
If no one is observing the statue, it will
move to a place immediately behind whoever

00:03:34.400 --> 00:03:38.560
is in the room with it, switching its pose
to a more threatening one.

00:03:38.560 --> 00:03:44.320
It moves silently, and no one has been able
to capture evidence of its method of locomotion.

00:03:44.320 --> 00:03:49.600
All that is known is that it does in fact
move, and it always appears extremely close

00:03:49.600 --> 00:03:54.480
to the subject of its interest, in order to
provoke a strong fight-or-flight reaction.

00:03:54.480 --> 00:03:59.920
The statue seems to have no interest in harming
those it frightens, never touching or directly

00:03:59.920 --> 00:04:01.600
interacting with anyone.

00:04:01.600 --> 00:04:07.760
It only seems interested in startling its
victims, if you can even call them “victims.”

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:12.640
It can be unpleasant to be unexpectedly frightened
like that, sure, but you get the same experience

00:04:12.640 --> 00:04:17.760
at most Halloween attractions or horror movies,
and people pay good money for those.

00:04:17.760 --> 00:04:22.320
Several trials were conducted in order to
determine the statue’s pattern of behavior.

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:26.720
In each trial, an SCP Foundation agent was
assigned to stand in the statue’s containment

00:04:26.720 --> 00:04:29.760
unit and watch the object for a period of
time.

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:34.480
When prompted by a researcher in another room,
speaking to them via radio, they were ordered

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:36.240
to look away from the statue.

00:04:36.240 --> 00:04:39.680
Once cleared to look at the statue again,
they were ordered to look around the room

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:42.720
and report where it went, and what it was
doing.

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:47.760
In most of the experiments, the statue appeared
directly behind the personnel, angled with

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:53.120
its arms reaching toward them and its head
glaring down at them, as if about to attack.

00:04:53.120 --> 00:04:57.680
In nearly every trial, the statue hit the
same position, and the Agent looking at it

00:04:57.680 --> 00:04:59.760
was startled to the point of screaming.

00:04:59.760 --> 00:05:03.280
There was even talk of cutting footage of
all of the screams together into a video that

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:05.680
would be shown at the company Christmas party.

00:05:05.680 --> 00:05:10.560
However, in three cases, the statue adopted
a different pose as well as position in the

00:05:10.560 --> 00:05:15.840
room, much to the surprise and confusion of
the team conducting the experiments.

00:05:15.840 --> 00:05:20.320
When Agent Dunne was assigned to observe the
statue, he was asked to close his eyes for

00:05:20.320 --> 00:05:24.080
five seconds and wait for SCP-650 to move.

00:05:24.080 --> 00:05:28.080
When he opened his eyes, the first thing he
did was whirl around and look behind him,

00:05:28.080 --> 00:05:30.960
having heard about the results of the previous
tests.

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:35.120
However, when he turned to face the statue,
there was nothing there.

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:39.360
He turned back around to his original stance,
preparing to radio Command and tell them the

00:05:39.360 --> 00:05:43.040
statue was gone, when he let out a yelp of
surprise.

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:47.040
There, at the table in the corner several
feet away, was the statue.

00:05:47.040 --> 00:05:52.160
It was lying on the table with its arms behind
its head, as if relaxing, with the area considered

00:05:52.160 --> 00:05:54.720
to be its “face” turned directly toward
Dunne.

00:05:54.720 --> 00:05:58.880
Unsettled by the surprise, and definitely
uncomfortable with how the statue seemed to

00:05:58.880 --> 00:06:02.560
be looking at him, he left the room without
another word.

00:06:02.560 --> 00:06:06.960
At another point in the trials, Agent Riley
pulled the short straw and was told to enter

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:08.560
650’s containment.

00:06:08.560 --> 00:06:12.880
She stood in the center of the room and stared
at the statue in front of her for a long period

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:13.680
of time.

00:06:13.680 --> 00:06:18.160
When given the command, she closed her eyes
and waited for a duration of 30 seconds.

00:06:18.160 --> 00:06:22.720
Much like Agent Dunne, her first instinct
on opening her eyes was to turn around and

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:26.080
look behind her, ready to see the statue there.

00:06:26.080 --> 00:06:30.160
Instead, however, it was sitting on a chair
at the other end of the room, the points where

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:32.960
its hands should be neatly folded in its lap.

00:06:32.960 --> 00:06:37.120
Its body was facing away from Agent Riley,
but even though she was looking at what could

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:41.520
have easily been the back of the statue’s
head, she later reported the distinct sense

00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:43.360
that it was looking at her.

00:06:43.360 --> 00:06:47.760
Though she didn’t scream like her colleagues
had when it was their turn to watch the statue,

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:52.880
she confessed to feeling an overwhelming sense
of unease, and her hands would not stop shaking

00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:54.960
for the next several hours.

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:59.920
These two instances of the statue adopting
a casual posture and keeping its distance

00:06:59.920 --> 00:07:05.120
from its observers were bizarre, but the final
break from the statue’s usual behavior was

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:06.800
the strangest of them all.

00:07:06.800 --> 00:07:12.000
Agent Cho was sent into SCP-650’s containment
and told to stand with his back against the

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:13.600
wall of his choice.

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:18.400
The plan was to determine what the statue
would do if its usual favorite position, just

00:07:18.400 --> 00:07:21.600
behind the observer, was no longer an option.

00:07:21.600 --> 00:07:26.800
If there was no space behind Agent Cho, then
the statue could not turn up there.

00:07:26.800 --> 00:07:31.120
Once he was settled into his spot and had
been watching the statue for several minutes,

00:07:31.120 --> 00:07:34.400
Agent Cho closed his eyes for exactly one
minute.

00:07:34.400 --> 00:07:38.960
When he opened them, he immediately scanned
the room to see where the statue had gone.

00:07:38.960 --> 00:07:43.840
It was not at the table or the chair, nor
was it standing in its original place in front

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:44.560
of him.

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:46.560
Finally, he spotted it.

00:07:46.560 --> 00:07:51.520
The statue was huddled in the corner of the
room, curled up in an approximation of the

00:07:51.520 --> 00:07:52.720
fetal position.

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:57.520
Its head was down, and its arms were held
up in front of its face as if trying to protect

00:07:57.520 --> 00:07:57.840
itself.

00:07:58.400 --> 00:08:03.120
Though he could not explain why, Agent Cho
got a distinct impression that the statue

00:08:03.120 --> 00:08:04.240
was afraid.

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:08.720
His stomach dropped at the sight, and he would
later admit to his supervisor that he briefly

00:08:08.720 --> 00:08:12.320
thought about trying to comfort SCP-650 somehow.

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:17.600
The impulse passed, but Cho was left with
a mixture of anxiety and guilt as if he had

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:20.160
done something wrong and upset the statue.

00:08:20.160 --> 00:08:23.920
The sensation did not pass until he was out
of the room.

00:08:23.920 --> 00:08:29.440
It is not entirely clear why the statue chose
these alternative poses during these particular

00:08:29.440 --> 00:08:30.480
experiments.

00:08:30.480 --> 00:08:34.560
The prevailing theory among the research team
is that these are simply other tools in its

00:08:34.560 --> 00:08:39.600
arsenal, methods that it can use to elicit
a strong reaction from a person who is less

00:08:39.600 --> 00:08:42.400
likely to be startled by its usual trick.

00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:48.960
Following the incident with Dr. Smith, SCP-650
was upgraded from Safe Class to Euclid Class.

00:08:48.960 --> 00:08:53.920
Just to clarify, for the people in the back:
Euclid Class SCP’s are not necessarily considered

00:08:53.920 --> 00:08:59.360
to be dangerous but require more effort to
contain than objects classified as Safe.

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:04.640
Most SCP’s that display autonomy or independent
thought, but are not overtly hostile toward

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:07.440
humanity, are classified as Euclid.

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:11.840
Along with its updated status, special containment
procedures have been employed in order to

00:09:11.840 --> 00:09:16.000
keep this Startling Statue from making any
more surprise escapes.

00:09:16.000 --> 00:09:21.200
SCP-650 is to be stored in a locked room,
4 meters by 4 meters.

00:09:21.200 --> 00:09:26.400
It is to be kept under constant surveillance
by at least three personnel at any given time,

00:09:26.400 --> 00:09:31.120
standing so that the SCP and at least one
of the observers are visible to them at all

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:32.000
times.

00:09:32.000 --> 00:09:36.880
They are allowed to watch the statue remotely,
via security camera, as long as they remain

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:38.640
focused on the SCP.

00:09:38.640 --> 00:09:41.920
This method is only to be employed in case
of emergency.

00:09:41.920 --> 00:09:46.240
A great deal of the Foundation budget was
dedicated to maintaining up-to-date containment

00:09:46.240 --> 00:09:50.720
facilities for SCP-650, as demanded in a note
from Dr. Smith.

00:09:50.720 --> 00:09:53.360
in the official file for SCP-650.

00:09:53.360 --> 00:09:57.840
The note reads: “I don't give a flying rat
about the budget; keep this damn thing contained!

00:09:57.840 --> 00:09:59.680
Turning around in a dim office to see this&nbsp;

00:09:59.680 --> 00:10:01.920
thing a half-inch away from&nbsp;
your nose is guaranteed

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:03.520
to take years from your life.

00:10:03.520 --> 00:10:06.960
And given what we deal with, we don't have
many to spare.”

00:10:06.960 --> 00:10:10.320
So, what does the Startling Statue want?

00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:15.360
Why does it use its power of mobility to scare
people but never do anything beyond that?

00:10:15.360 --> 00:10:19.520
No one is certain, and the Foundation has
too many other fires to put out to bother

00:10:19.520 --> 00:10:22.320
looking further into a clearly benign entity.

00:10:22.320 --> 00:10:27.600
Unfortunately, there are questions about SCP-650
that will never be answered, and there is

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:30.080
so much about it we will never know.

00:10:30.080 --> 00:10:31.680
One thing is for sure, though.

00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:36.240
If you find yourself alone in a room with
an unsettling statue, you had better keep

00:10:36.240 --> 00:10:37.280
an eye on it.

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:38.640
Just in case.

00:10:38.640 --> 00:10:46.800
Now go check out “SCP-173 Origin Story - How
173 Got to Site-19” and “SCP-689 - Haunter

00:10:46.800 --> 00:10:51.760
In The Dark” for more of the SCP Foundation’s
strange and frightening statues!

